  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds access in the hpmud DOT4 and MLC\n     transports (ELSCVE-271050)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91101.patch (since els1)\n     - CVE-2026-91101\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: unchecked MFPDTF block length in the hpaio backend\n     (ELSCVE-271051)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91103.patch (since els1)\n     - CVE-2026-91103\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap overflow in the hpcups raster line buffer\n     (ELSCVE-271046)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91104.patch (since els1)\n     - CVE-2026-91104\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: buffer overflows in the hpps filter (ELSCVE-271049)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91105.patch (since els1)\n     - CVE-2026-91105\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: buffer overflows in hpcups, hpijs and the hpaio HTTP\n     response reader (ELSCVE-271045)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91106.patch (since els1)\n     - CVE-2026-91106\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: insecure lock file used by hpssd to start the HP\n     plug-in installer (ELSCVE-271048)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91099.patch (since els2)\n     - CVE-2026-91099\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: lp/lpr argument injection via the file name in hp-print\n     (ELSCVE-271047)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-91102.patch (since els2)\n     - CVE-2026-91102\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: remaining HPLIP 3.26.6 security fixes (advisory\n     HPSBPI04151)\n     - debian/patches/hplip-3.26.6-security-remainder.patch: bound copies,\n       indexes and sizes in libhpmud (pml, hpmud, jd, model, musb), hpijs,\n       hp_ipp addCupsPrinter() and the hpaio scan backends; quote the input\n       file name in pstotiff; check the user name and create a private fax\n       FIFO in the hpfax backend; confine HP plug-in install paths; clean up\n       device model names.\n     - debian/patches/hplip-3.26.6-pkservice-removal.patch, debian/rules,\n       debian/hplip.install, debian/hplip.manpages: remove the root\n       hp-pkservice D-Bus service, its D-Bus and polkit files and\n       --enable-policykit; non-root HP plug-in installs keep using su/sudo;\n       downstream: keep base/pkit.py, which HP's 3.17.10 plug-in installer\n       imports.\n     - Behaviour change: PC-fax through the hpfax backend now hangs the fax\n       queue until the job is cancelled (its FIFO is 0600, owned by lp).\n     - Behaviour change: tools run as root (sudo hp-setup in GUI mode,\n       hp-toolbox) hang when they need the HP plug-in (hp-plugin waits on a\n       terminal nobody answers); run hp-plugin from a terminal instead.",
